module std where

-- =========================================================================
-- Real ⇄ Rational / Real ⇄ Number / Real ⇄ ℝ-refinement bridges (numeric-tower
-- Phase 4).
--
-- The opaque-boundary crossings the D7 law, the Reprable instance, and the D8 iso
-- need. `Real` is `$opaque { repr:"real", pure: Real seq … modulus … converges … }`:
-- the runtime value is the function-record (there is NO JS-native real); the
-- Reprable native is a `Number` SAMPLE of the sequence at a fixed precision (FAR
-- lossier than Rational — a double cannot round-trip a real; it is a sample at one
-- precision, the D7 ℝ carve-out made total). These bridges embed / sample the
-- structure so the pure bodies (real-arith.fenel) can be exercised against the
-- native rep on small samples. They compose the Phase-3 Rational bridges
-- (numberToRational / rationalToNumber) + the Phase-1 Nat bridge (numberToNat).
--
--   ratToReal    : Rational -> Real   the ℚ↪ℝ embedding (constant sequence).
--   numberToReal : Number   -> Real   = ratToReal ∘ numberToRational (the lower).
--   realToNumber : Real     -> Number  sample seq at modulus(PREC) (the lossy lift).
--
-- ratToReal IS THE PRINCIPLED ENTRY. A Real of value q is the CONSTANT sequence
-- `seq n = q` with `modulus k = Zero` (every term IS the limit ⇒ trivially Cauchy,
-- modulus 0 at every precision). This is the rational embedding ℚ ⊂ ℝ that the
-- SUBTYPE_LATTICE Rational⊂Real row names — the natural way to construct a Real,
-- and what the tests build their reals from (exact, since the seq is the exact
-- Rational). numberToReal composes it (numberToRational floors to the integer
-- Number domain — the Phase-3 bridge contract — so numberToReal is faithful over
-- ℤ-valued Numbers; non-integer Reals are built via ratToReal directly).

@label "Rational to Real"
@description "The ℚ↪ℝ embedding: a Real whose value is the Rational q, as the CONSTANT sequence seq n = q with modulus k = Zero (every term is the limit ⇒ trivially Cauchy, modulus 0). The principled Real constructor (matches the SUBTYPE_LATTICE Rational⊂Real row); numberToReal and the tests build reals from it. converges = CauchyAx (the constant-sequence convergence is the simplest discharge)."
@tags "numeric" "real" "bridge" "embedding"
ratToReal : (q: Rational) -> Real
ratToReal q = Real { seq = \n -> q, modulus = \k -> Zero, converges = CauchyAx }

@label "Number to Real"
@description "Materialize a Number as a Real via the rational embedding: numberToReal x = ratToReal (numberToRational x). Faithful over the integer Number domain (numberToRational floors fractional parts — the Phase-3 bridge contract; non-integer reals are constructed with ratToReal over an exact Rational). The LOWER of the Reprable JsRuntime/Jsonb Real instances."
@tags "numeric" "real" "bridge"
numberToReal : (x: Number) -> Real
numberToReal x = ratToReal (numberToRational x)

@label "Real to Number"
@description "Sample a Real to a Number (the LOSSY projection, the D7 ℝ carve-out): realToNumber r = rationalToNumber (r.seq (r.modulus PREC)) at a fixed precision PREC = 30 (≈ 2^30 ≈ 1e9, ~double precision). For a constant-sequence (ratToReal / numberToReal) real the modulus is Zero so the sample is the exact embedded Rational; for an arithmetic result the modulus selects the sampling index. The LIFT of the Reprable JsRuntime/Jsonb Real instances — a Number is a SAMPLE of the real at one precision, never an exact round-trippable rep (unlike the finite rungs)."
@tags "numeric" "real" "bridge"
realToNumber : (r: Real) -> Number
realToNumber r = case r of
  Real { seq = s, modulus = m, converges = c } -> rationalToNumber (s (m (numberToNat 30)))

-- D8 — the inductive↔refinement iso witnesses (Real ≅ { x: Number | isReal x }).
-- numeric-tower audit §3 D8: each rung has an inductive presentation (the Cauchy
-- Σ-type) AND a refinement presentation (Real-as-a-refinement-of-Number = ℝ),
-- connected by an iso = a witness PAIR + the round-trip laws (proof = inhabitant —
-- [[feedback_laws_supers_are_el_dependent_typing]]), NOT a `Presentations` class.
--
-- THE FIRST RUNG WHERE THE TWO PRESENTATIONS DIVERGE IN DECIDABILITY (north-star
-- §3/§6/§9). The inductive (Cauchy) presentation's equality is PARTIAL (realEq →
-- Maybe Bool); the refinement (ℝ set) presentation's interval membership is
-- `Tri`-partial over ℝ. Below this rung the two presentations agreed (decidable
-- both ways); ℝ is the canonical exercise of the substrate's Nothing/Tri boundary.
--
-- CODOMAIN — CLOSED (containment-substrate Phase 3, the top-of-tower closure).
-- The precise refinement codomain is `{ x: Number | isReal x }` (= the finite-real
-- set the membershipReal decider recognizes); the numeric tower (Phase 4) left it
-- stubbed as `Number`. containment-substrate Phase 3 registered it — `RealNumber =
-- Number | value ∈ ℝ` (foundation.fenel; ℝ = membershipReal, the finite reals).
-- This is ℝ's refinement presentation — a (mild) PROPER refinement of Number
-- (membershipReal excludes NaN/±Inf), recorded honestly as NOT a bare identity.
-- The witnesses are now retyped onto that codomain (cheap = the re-typed sample
-- bridges; the BODY is unchanged). This is the FIRST rung where the two
-- presentations diverge in decidability (Cauchy eq partial; ℝ interval membership
-- Tri-partial) — the alias names the refinement side of that divergence. The
-- round-trip laws —
--   realFromRefined (realToRefined r) ≡ r   (Real side, over exact-sample reals)
--   realToRefined (realFromRefined n) ≡ n   (refinement side, over integer n)
-- are stated here and sample-discharged in real-tower.test.ts; their `$el`
-- law-field home on the rung type lands with the Phase-5 class minting (the same
-- deferral as the D7 law). Standalone from D5 (D8c′).

@label "Real to ℝ-refinement"
@description "Iso witness (D8): the Real ⇄ ℝ refinement view. realToRefined = realToNumber re-typed onto the real refinement of Number. CODOMAIN CLOSED (containment-substrate Phase 3): the precise codomain `RealNumber = Number | value ∈ ℝ` is now a registered alias (foundation.fenel; ℝ = membershipReal, the finite reals — a mild PROPER refinement, not bare identity). This is the FIRST rung where the inductive↔refinement presentations diverge in decidability (Cauchy eq partial; ℝ interval membership Tri-partial). Pairs with realFromRefined; round-trips over the exact-sample sub-domain (sample-discharged Phase 4, $el law field Phase 5)."
@tags "numeric" "real" "iso"
realToRefined : (r: Real) -> RealNumber
realToRefined r = realToNumber r

@label "ℝ-refinement to Real"
@description "Iso witness (D8): the inverse of realToRefined. realFromRefined = numberToReal over the real-refined domain `RealNumber = Number | value ∈ ℝ` (CLOSED, containment-substrate Phase 3; see realToRefined). Pairs with realToRefined."
@tags "numeric" "real" "iso"
realFromRefined : (n: RealNumber) -> Real
realFromRefined n = numberToReal n
